<title>USA: CME July pork bellies fall limit on local sales.</title>
<headline>CME July pork bellies fall limit on local sales.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME July pork bellies fell their 3.00-cent limit near the close Friday on local and technical selling, traders said.</p>
<p>A weaker cash pork belly market at noon CDT fueled the downturn. Cargill was a noted seller on the break, according to traders.</p>
<p>At 1256, July bellies were down 2.650 cent at 84.500 cents a lb, with the rest 1.300 to 2.550 lower.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
